  "machines": 4,
  "setup": "Head (rank 0, API) + three workers (ranks 1-3, --headless, same args with their NODE_RANK) over the CX7 RoCE fabric (--nnodes 4). Set NODE_RANK, HEAD_IP, NODE_IP, CX7_IF and CX7_IB per node; NODE_IP must be the node's fabric IPv4 and NCCL_IB_HCA must list the RDMA device of the fabric interface first. Every node downloads the pinned 0xSero/Step-5-Preview-Spark repository (~342 GB, files under ~5 GiB, no reassembly) to local NVMe and mounts it read-only at /model. Mount a persistent /cache for compile and RoCE caches; clear /cache/vllm/torch_compile_cache after changing body format, MTP or graph settings. VLLM_DISABLE_SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM=1 is required (a shared-expert side stream deadlocks the EXL3 MoE kernel). Run a host memory guard on every node (GB10 unified memory; github.com/0xSero/Step-5-Preview-Four-Sparks scripts/memguard.sh). Load ~12-13 minutes. KV 20 GB per rank = 999,279 tokens at 262,144 context. Validated: all six lab gates pass on four DGX Sparks (2026-10-06).",
  "source": "https://github.com/0xSero/local-ai-images/tree/main/step-5-preview-spark",
